   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# broll-wan22-flf\nWan 2.2 14B first/last-frame to video, full 20 steps (10 high-noise + 10 low-noise), no LoRA.\nFor B-roll, walking shots, wides: anything with no lip sync. Wan generates **no audio**; cut it against the mix.\n\n**Inputs:** `in_start_image`, `in_end_image`, `in_prompt` (Wan follows camera and motion language well, keep\nappearance words light: the frames carry the look), `in_seconds` (clip length; frames = 4n+1 at 16 fps).\n`in_size` sets width x height. Native: 1280x720 (16:9) or 720x1280 (9:16). 81 frames (5 s) is what Wan was trained on;\nlonger clips loop or drift.\n\n**Frame rate:** Wan renders 16 fps. For the 24 fps edit, interpolate (RIFE in comfyui-frame-interpolation) or let\nCapCut conform it.\n\nSpeed: about 15-25 min per 5 s clip at 1280x720 on a 4090. For drafts, the official template\n`video_wan2_2_14B_flf2v` has a 4-step lightx2v path (~3 min) with weaker motion and detail."
   ],
   "title": "broll-wan22-flf: how to use"
  }
